Repair the complete TypeScript source below and return a corrected complete source file with the same exports. `GalleryModel` requires at least one nonempty trimmed image ID and rejects any duplicate after trimming. It starts at the first image and the `summary` tab. `next` and `previous` wrap in input order. `selectTab` changes the tab. `snapshot` returns detached data. Invalid construction throws `TypeError` without modifying the input, and caller mutation of either constructor input or snapshots must not affect the model.

Known-bad source:
```typescript
export type GalleryTab = "summary" | "notes" | "owner";
export interface GallerySnapshot { readonly image: string; readonly index: number; readonly tab: GalleryTab; readonly images: readonly string[]; }

export class GalleryModel {
  private readonly images: string[];
  private index = 0;
  private tab: GalleryTab = "summary";

  constructor(images: readonly string[]) {
    if (images.length === 0) throw new TypeError("images required");
    this.images = images.map(image => image.trim());
    if (this.images.some(image => !image) || new Set(this.images).size !== this.images.length) throw new TypeError("invalid images");
  }

  next(): void { this.index = (this.index + 1) % (this.images.length - 1); }
  previous(): void { this.index = (this.index - 1 + this.images.length) % this.images.length; }
  selectTab(tab: GalleryTab): void { this.tab = tab; }

  snapshot(): GallerySnapshot {
    return { image: this.images[this.index], index: this.index, tab: this.tab, images: [...this.images] };
  }
}
```

